PlainMemory

Design references:
- OpenViking — Beijing Volcano Engine Technology Co., Ltd. / Volcengine contributors
  https://github.com/volcengine/OpenViking
  Local reference license: Apache-2.0
- DeepRead — authors/contributors identified in the upstream repository
  https://github.com/zhangqianyizhn/DeepRead
  Local reference license: Apache-2.0

PlainMemory is an independent minimal Python implementation. It retains the
HTTP/service separation, explicit user scoping, and normalized dense retrieval
ideas, removes the full context filesystem, semantic extraction and Agent stack,
uses SQLite atomic ingestion, and replaces weighted hybrid fusion with stable
vector-first/BM25-second interleaving. The upstream projects are not runtime
dependencies. Referenced licenses and original authors must be retained if code
from those projects is copied into future versions.
